{
  "id": "secret_usage",
  "type": "relationship",
  "question": "How does a Pod reference a Secret for use as an environment variable in the Kubernetes API schema?",
  "resource": "io.k8s.api.core.v1.PodSpec",
  "scope": "Namespaced",
  "multi_hop": true,
  "ground_truth": {
    "answer": "PodSpec references a Secret at two levels. At the high level, PodSpec has a USES_SECRET edge to Secret, representing that the Pod depends on the Secret resource. At the field level, the path is: PodSpec -[HAS_CONTAINER]-> Container -[HAS_PROPERTY]-> EnvVar -[HAS_PROPERTY]-> EnvVarSource. EnvVarSource.secretKeyRef is a SecretKeySelector with name (the Secret object name) and key (the specific data key within that Secret). Alternatively, SecretVolumeSource can be used to mount a Secret as a volume. The Secret must reside in the same namespace as the Pod.",
    "context": [
      "io.k8s.api.core.v1.PodSpec: containers field (HAS_CONTAINER) links to Container objects; USES_SECRET edge to Secret captures the dependency at the Pod level",
      "io.k8s.api.core.v1.EnvVarSource: source for an environment variable value; secretKeyRef field (SecretKeySelector) references a key within a named Secret",
      "io.k8s.api.core.v1.SecretKeySelector: selects a key from a Secret by name and key fields"
    ],
